  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Should You Build a Detached ADU or Choose a Room Addition?",
    "text": "Should You Build a Detached ADU or Choose a Room Addition?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "A detached ADU may be a strong fit when a San Diego-area homeowner needs independent living space and the lot can support the required building envelope, access, utilities, and approvals. The right choice depends on site constraints, intended occupancy, privacy, construction complexity, and whether a room addition or garage conversion would meet the same goal more efficiently.",
